msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:84
msgid "Logging all but the first time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:86
msgid ""
"The following code will output a log message from a ROS 2 node at ``WARN`` "
"severity, but not the very first time it is hit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:92
msgid ""
"// printf style\n"
"RCLCPP_WARN_SKIPFIRST(node->get_logger(), \"My log message %d\", 4);\n"
"\n"
"// C++ stream style\n"
"RCLCPP_WARN_STREAM_SKIPFIRST(node->get_logger(), \"My log message \" << 4);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:102
msgid ""
"num = 4\n"
"node.get_logger().warning('My log message {0}'.format(num), skip_first=True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:108
msgid "Logging throttled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:110
msgid ""
"The following code will output a log message from a ROS 2 node at ``ERROR`` "
"severity, but no more than once per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:112
msgid ""
"The interval parameter specifying milliseconds between messages should have "
"an integer data type so it can be converted to a "
"``rcutils_duration_value_t`` (an ``int64_t``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:118
msgid ""
"// printf style\n"
"RCLCPP_ERROR_THROTTLE(node->get_logger(), *node->get_clock(), 1000, \"My log "
"message %d\", 4);\n"
"\n"
"// C++ stream style\n"
"RCLCPP_ERROR_STREAM_THROTTLE(node->get_logger(), *node->get_clock(), 1000, "
"\"My log message \" << 4);\n"
"\n"
"// For now, use the nanoseconds() method to use an existing rclcpp::Duration "
"value, see https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/issues/1929\n"
"RCLCPP_ERROR_STREAM_THROTTLE(node->get_logger(), *node->get_clock(), "
"msg_interval.nanoseconds()/1000000, \"My log message \" << 4);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:131
msgid ""
"num = 4\n"
"node.get_logger().error(f'My log message {num}', throttle_duration_sec=1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:137
msgid "Logging throttled all but the first time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:139
msgid ""
"The following code will output a log message from a ROS 2 node at ``DEBUG`` "
"severity, no more than once per second, skipping the very first time it is "
"hit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:145
msgid ""
"// printf style\n"
"RCLCPP_DEBUG_SKIPFIRST_THROTTLE(node->get_logger(), *node->get_clock(), "
"1000, \"My log message %d\", 4);\n"
"\n"
"RCLCPP_DEBUG_SKIPFIRST_THROTTLE(node->get_logger(), *node->get_clock(), "
"1000, \"My log message \" << 4);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:154
msgid ""
"num = 4\n"
"node.get_logger().debug(f'My log message {num}', skip_first=True, "
"throttle_duration_sec=1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:160
msgid "Logging demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:162
msgid ""
"In this `demo <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/rolling/logging_demo>`_, "
"different types of log calls are shown and the severity level of different "
"loggers is configured locally and externally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:164
msgid "Start the demo with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:166
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:528
msgid "$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:170
msgid ""
"Over time you will see output from various log calls with different "
"properties. To start with you will only see output from log calls with "
"severity ``INFO`` and above (``WARN``, ``ERROR``, ``FATAL``). Note that the "
"first message will only be logged once, though the line is reached on each "
"iteration, as that is a property of the log call used for that message."
