#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:333
msgid "Using the logger config component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:335
msgid ""
"The server that responds to the logger configuration requests has been "
"developed as a component so that it may be added to an existing composition-"
"based system. For example, if you are using `a container to run your nodes "
"<../../ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Composition>`, to be able to configure your "
"loggers you only need to request that it additionally load the "
"``logging_demo::LoggerConfig`` component into the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:338
msgid ""
"As an example, if you want to debug the ``composition::Talker`` demo, you "
"can start the talker as normal with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:340
msgid "Shell 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:342
msgid "$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:346
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:363
msgid "Shell 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:348
msgid "$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:352
msgid ""
"And then when you want to enable debug logging, load the ``LoggerConfig`` "
"component with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:354
msgid "Shell 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:356
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager logging_demo logging_demo::"
"LoggerConfig"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:360
msgid ""
"And finally, configure all unset loggers to the debug severity by addressing "
"the empty-named logger. Note that loggers that have been specifically "
"configured to use a particular severity will not be affected by this call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:365
msgid ""
"$ ros2 service call /config_logger logging_demo/srv/ConfigLogger "
"\"{logger_name: '', level: DEBUG}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:369
msgid ""
"You should see debug output from any previously unset loggers in the process "
"start to appear, including from the ROS 2 core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:372
msgid "Logger level configuration: command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:374
msgid ""
"As of the Bouncy ROS 2 release, the severity level for loggers that have not "
"had their severity set explicitly can be configured from the command line. "
"Restart the demo including the following command line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:378
msgid "$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main --ros-args --log-level debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:382
msgid ""
"This configures the default severity for any unset logger to the debug "
"severity level. You should see debug output from loggers from the demo "
"itself and from the ROS 2 core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:385
msgid ""
"The severity level for individual loggers can be configured from the command-"
"line. Restart the demo including the following command line arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:388
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main --ros-args --log-level "
"logger_usage_demo:=debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:394
msgid "Console output formatting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:396
msgid ""
"If you would like more or less verbose formatting, you can use the "
"``RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT`` environment variable. For example, to "
"additionally get the timestamp and location of the log calls, stop the demo "
"and restart it with the environment variable set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:403
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:410
msgid ""
"$ export RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT=\"[{severity} {time}] [{name}]: "
"{message} ({function_name}() at {file_name}:{line_number})\"\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:417
msgid ""
"$ set \"RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT=[{severity} {time}] [{name}]: "
"{message} ({function_name}() at {file_name}:{line_number})\"\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:422
msgid ""
"You should see the timestamp in seconds and the function name, filename and "
"line number additionally printed with each message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:424
msgid ""
"For more information on configuring the console logger formatting, see the :"
"ref:`logger console configuration <logging-configuration-environment-"
"variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:427
msgid "Console output colorizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:429
msgid ""
"By default, the output is colorized when it's targeting a terminal. If you "
"would like to force enabling or disabling it, you can use the "
"``RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT`` environment variable. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:437
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:444
msgid ""
"$ export RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=0  # 1 for forcing it\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:451
msgid ""
"$ set \"RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=0\" :: 1 for forcing it\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:456
msgid ""
"You should see that debug, warn, error and fatal logs aren't colorized now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:460
msgid ""
"In Linux and MacOS forcing colorized output means that if you redirect the "
"output to a file, the ansi escape color codes will appear on it. In windows "
"the colorization method relies on console APIs. If it is forced you will get "
"a new warning saying that colorization failed. The default behavior already "
"checks if the output is a console or not, so forcing colorization is not "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:467
msgid ""
"If you start several nodes via ``ros2 launch``, no node has an active "
"terminal attached to it (unless you set ``emulate_tty=True``). This means "
"that to get colorized output for ``ros2 launch``, you need to set "
"``RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=1`` explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:471
msgid "Default stream for console output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:473
msgid ""
"In Foxy and later, the output from all debug levels goes to stderr by "
"default. It is possible to force all output to go to stdout by setting the "
"``RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT`` environment variable to ``1``. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:481
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:487
msgid "$ export RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:493
msgid "$ set \"RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT=1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:499
msgid "Line buffered console output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:502
msgid ""
"By default, all logging output is unbuffered. You can force it to be "
"buffered by setting the ``RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM`` environment "
"variable to 1. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:510
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:516
msgid "$ export RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:522
msgid "$ set \"RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM=1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:526
msgid "Then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:533
msgid "Setting the log file name prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:535
msgid ""
"By default, the log file name is based on the executable file name followed "
"by process ID and system timestamp on file creation. You can change the log "
"file name prefix to one of your choice using the ``--log-file-name`` command "
"line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:538
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker --ros-args --log-file-name filename"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:542
msgid ""
"This configures the log file name prefix to ``filename``, instead of the "
"executable file name (which is ``talker`` in this case)."
msgstr ""
